# Git Commits – Use Repository Owner Identity

When making git commits in this project:

- **Never** set the commit author to "Cursor Agent", "Cursor", "AI", or any bot/assistant identity.
- **Always** use the repository owner's identity for author and committer:
  - Run `git config user.name` and `git config user.email` in the project to get the configured identity.
  - Use that name and email for any commits (e.g. when suggesting commit messages or when the user runs commits from Cursor).
- If you are asked to run `git commit`, use the existing git config; do not override with an agent or bot identity.

The human repository owner should be the only contributor listed for commits in this project.
